1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:03,282
(Bernadette:)What is it about trains
that you like so much?

2
00:00:03,281 --> 00:00:05,451
(Sheldon:)What an interesting
question.

3
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:08,420
(Sheldon:)When I was a child,
life was confusing

4
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:11,420
(Sheldon:)and chaotic for me, and
trains represented order.

5
00:00:11,423 --> 00:00:15,463
(Sheldon:)I could line them up,
categorize them, control them.

6
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:16,960
(Sheldon:)I guess you
could say that

7
00:00:16,962 --> 00:00:20,392
(Sheldon:)they gave me a sense of calm
in a world that didn't.

8
00:00:20,398 --> 00:00:22,468
(Bernadette:)That's lovely, Sheldon.

9
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:25,167
(Sheldon:)Well... other than when they're
chugging through your bowels,

10
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:27,000
(Sheldon:)these things are magic.

11
00:00:30,008 --> 00:00:31,978
(Leonard:)I have to admit,
I've been worried about

12
00:00:31,977 --> 00:00:34,977
(Leonard:)the military applications since
we started talking about this.

13
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,350
(Howard:)Me, too.

14
00:00:36,348 --> 00:00:37,678
(Leonard:)Why didn't you
say something?

15
00:00:37,682 --> 00:00:40,112
(Howard:)Same reason I don't
talk about ass cancer.

16
00:00:40,118 --> 00:00:43,088
(Howard:)It's not a
pleasant topic.

17
00:00:43,088 --> 00:00:44,658
(Raj:)You can't let this stop you.

18
00:00:44,656 --> 00:00:46,686
(Raj:)Almost any scientific
advancement can be used

19
00:00:46,691 --> 00:00:48,391
(Raj:)for destructive purposes.

20
00:00:48,393 --> 00:00:50,423
(Amy:)It's true. Even Einstein's
theory of relativity

21
00:00:50,428 --> 00:00:53,098
(Amy:)was later applied to the
development of nuclear weapons.

22
00:00:53,098 --> 00:00:54,928
(Penny:)E equals MC squared.

23
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:56,303
(Sheldon:)Yeah.

24
00:00:56,301 --> 00:00:57,631
“E” is for energy,
“M” for mass,

25
00:00:57,636 --> 00:00:59,066
and “C” for the speed of light.

